      "text": "The internal supply voltage V , is derived from the int external V , as shown by ext this measurement result. The value of about 1.2–1.3 V depends obviously on the actual values of V . They must be about T 100 mV lower than for the previous rail-to-rail amplifier. The minimum external supply voltage is little more than the internal one, about 100 mV higher. This means that this amplifier can be used with an external supply voltage from 1.3 V. The maximum external supply voltage is limited however. Folded cascodes can only go about 0.5 V above the positive supply voltage. The rail-to-rail performance is therefore limited to approximately 1.8 V."
